<script>
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import HeaderMenus from './lib/HeaderMenus.abide'
import headerMenus from './lib/HeaderMenus.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import IconMenu from './lib/IconMenu.abide'
import iconMenu from './lib/IconMenu.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import MoveStage from './lib/MoveStage.abide'
import moveStage from './lib/MoveStage.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import MoveSubmenu from './lib/MoveSubmenu.abide'
import moveSubmenu from './lib/MoveSubmenu.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import OpenElsewhere from './lib/OpenElsewhere.abide'
import openElsewhere from './lib/OpenElsewhere.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import OpenLayout from './lib/OpenLayout.abide'
import openLayout from './lib/OpenLayout.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import PinDeal from './lib/PinDeal.abide'
import pinDeal from './lib/PinDeal.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/headless/toolbar', '/headless/popover', '/behaviors/hotkeys']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealSubmenu.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('ArrowRight opens a submenu, and ArrowDown walks past it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealSubmenu.test.ts',
            from: ["test('ArrowLeft or Escape closes the submenu alone'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealSubmenu.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a pick in a submenu closes every menu, and its trigger item opens it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealSubmenu.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the outer menu closing closes its submenu'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/menu.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('Tab in a submenu standing apart closes it and the menu it opened from",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealActions.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the arrow keys skip the stage the deal is in'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealActions.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a pick moves the deal and hands focus back'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealActions.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a checkbox item changes its state and leaves the menu open'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/deals/lib/DealActions.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('typing moves focus to the item whose text starts with it'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/menu.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('open written by the app opens the menu at its first item",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/menu.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a mouse resting on the trigger opens the menu after openOnHover",
                "test('a menu a pointer opened closes once the pointer has left",
                "test('a group switches to the menu whose trigger the pointer enters",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Move a deal to another stage from a menu">
        <p>Spread <code>trigger</code> on a button and <code>menu</code> on the element holding
            the items. Each child carrying <code>role="menuitem"</code> is an item. A disabled
            one is passed over by the arrow keys, and a pick runs its own <code>onclick</code>,
            closes the menu and hands focus back to the button.</p>
        <Example code={moveStage}><MoveStage /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Open a submenu from an item">
        <p>Spread a second menu's <code>trigger</code> on an item carrying
            <code>role="menuitem"</code>, and that menu is a submenu of the one holding the item.
            Give it <code>side: 'right'</code>, and ArrowRight opens it while ArrowLeft closes it,
            back to its item. A pick in it closes every menu and hands focus to the first
            button.</p>
        <Example code={moveSubmenu}><MoveSubmenu /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Open a menu from an icon">
        <p>The trigger is your own element, so it holds anything, and its
            <code>aria-label</code> names the menu. <code>menu</code> takes the options a
            <code>popover</code> does, so <code>align: 'end'</code> lines it up with the icon's
            end.</p>
        <Example code={iconMenu}><IconMenu /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Pin a deal from a menu that stays open">
        <p>An item carrying <code>role="menuitemcheckbox"</code> or
            <code>role="menuitemradio"</code> leaves the menu open. Write its
            <code>aria-checked</code> from your own state.</p>
        <Example code={pinDeal}><PinDeal /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Open a menu from somewhere else">
        <p>Hand <code>menu</code> a <code>Reactive</code> as <code>open</code>, and spread its
            <code>anchor</code> on what the menu opens against. Writing it opens and closes the
            menu, and every way the menu closes writes it back.</p>
        <Example code={openElsewhere}><OpenElsewhere /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Lay out an open menu while a closed menu stays hidden">
        <p>The menu is a popover. A <code>display</code> class beats the browser's hiding of a
            closed popover, so set it behind <code>open:</code>.</p>
        <Example code={openLayout}><OpenLayout /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Switch between a header's menus on hover">
        <p>Give menus one <code>group</code>. Once one is open, the pointer on another's trigger
            opens it at once, and ArrowLeft and ArrowRight step between them.
            <code>openOnHover</code> opens one when a mouse rests on its trigger, and
            <code>closeOnLeave</code> closes a menu a pointer opened once the pointer has left it.
            A menu a key opened stays open. The menu switched to carries <code>data-from</code>,
            the side the last one stood on, so it can slide in from there. For an app's menubar,
            whose buttons share one tab stop, see <code>toolbar</code>.</p>
        <p>For a site's navigation links, a disclosure — a <code>popover</code> opened by a
            button — reads better to a screen reader than a menu, which announces commands.</p>
        <Example code={headerMenus}><HeaderMenus /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Jump to an item by typing">
        <p>A letter typed in an open menu moves focus to the next item starting with it, and
            letters typed together find the first item starting with the word.</p>
    </Section>
</Doc>
